---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import PullQuote from '../components/PullQuote.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Sarah Bowles is a Trainee Clinical Psychologist whose path into the field started with economics, teaching, and counselling in London and Hong Kong."
  pathname="/about"
>
  <PageHero
    title="About"
    eyebrow="Sarah Bowles, Trainee Clinical Psychologist"
  />

  <div class="container" style="padding-top: 2rem; padding-bottom: 2.5rem">
    <div style="max-width: 68ch" class="space-y-8">

      <PullQuote text='"I wanted to contribute to more systemic change in mental health."' />

      <Prose>
        <p>
          I'm a Trainee Clinical Psychologist in the final year of the Doctoral Programme in
          Clinical Psychology at the Salomons Institute for Applied Psychology, Canterbury Christ
          Church University. My doctoral research focuses on how mental health professionals can
          recognise and support growth following psychosis, exploring how clinicians understand
          growth, what they do to facilitate it, and how this might shape clinical practice.
        </p>
        <p>
          My path into clinical psychology was anything but linear, and that route has shaped how I
          think about what good mental health practice looks like.
        </p>
        <p>
          I first trained as an economist at the London School of Economics, drawn to the subject
          because I wanted to understand how to solve social problems. The further I went, the more
          I realised I wanted to work with people directly, so I trained as a teacher and spent
          several years teaching economics in London, where I became a pastoral form tutor and
          developed an emotional resilience programme for the school curriculum.
        </p>
        <p>
          Teaching brought me close to young people's emotional lives, and I realised that this was
          where my real interest lay. I retrained in psychology with an MSc at Kingston University,
          then completed an MA in Relationship Therapy through Relate and Hull University. Through
          this period I worked across a range of settings: as a counsellor at Relate providing
          individual, couple and family therapy; as a pastoral support worker in a London
          comprehensive; and as an assistant psychologist with the Complex Needs Outreach Team at
          the Tavistock and Portman NHS Foundation Trust and at the Brandon Centre.
        </p>
        <p>
          I later moved to Hong Kong, where I worked at{' '}
          <a href="https://www.sjccs.hk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">St John's Cathedral Counselling Service</a>
          , one of the city's largest mental health NGOs. After returning to the UK and having my
          daughter, I wanted to contribute to more systemic change in mental health, and this is
          what led me to apply for the Doctorate in Clinical Psychology.
        </p>
      </Prose>

      <section aria-labelledby="education-heading">
        <SectionHeading title="Education" />
        <div class="mt-8 space-y-8">
          <div>
            <p class="font-body font-medium text-base text-ink">Doctorate in Clinical Psychology (in progress)</p>
            <p class="font-body text-base text-muted mt-1">Salomons Institute for Applied Psychology, Canterbury Christ Church University</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-body font-medium text-base text-ink">MA Relationship Therapy (Distinction)</p>
            <p class="font-body text-base text-muted mt-1">Relate, validated by Hull University, accredited by BACP</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-body font-medium text-base text-ink">MSc Psychology (Distinction, with scholarship for academic excellence)</p>
            <p class="font-body text-base text-muted mt-1">Kingston University, BPS-accredited</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-body font-medium text-base text-ink">BSc Economics (First Class Honours, prize for outstanding academic merit)</p>
            <p class="font-body text-base text-muted mt-1">London School of Economics</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
